ys general enforce it.\n  - That rules out rung 1, \"without government interference\".\n  - It isn't rung 3: the bill makes no one liable for harm the system causes.\n  - It isn't rung 4: there is no testing before use.\n  - The annex says a bill that only requires disclosure fits no rung.\n- **AWARE Act (H.R. 5360), which she sponsored:** it has the FTC write educational material for parents and minors. Those aren't safety guidelines for AI companies, so it doesn't reach rung 2. I coded it adjacent.\n- **Her two press releases:** her quoted words name no oversight measure, so they show no position on the ladder.\n\n**`needs_source`:**\n- her recorded vote on H.R. 7757 (the KIDS Act) at the Energy and Commerce committee markup;\n- her own words on holding AI developers liable, testing AI before use, or requiring approval.\n\nThe one quote I coded looks back at her bill rather than saying what she would do. I marked it tier `none`, not quotable, with code `not-forward`.","ttft_ms":16959,"type":"result","duration_ms":39862,"uuid":"3b66bcda-30be-4f4c-be4c-edefa534c53f","ttft_stream_ms":2024,"time_to_request_ms":640,"first_content_frame_ms":2025,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
